      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "# The Lay of the Land: Toronto Maple Leafs\n\nAnother spring has passed without a playoff appearance. The Maple Leafs finished 32-36-14, eighth in the Atlantic Division, 31 games behind the pace-setter - a chasm that tells the whole story. <strong>The season ended not with a bang but with a seven-game losing streak</strong>, the kind of collapse that haunts front offices through the summer. Seventy-eight points and a 15th playoff seed that doesn't exist - this is what rebuilding looks like when it's been going on too long.\n\nThe roster questions are now unavoidable. Who stays? Who leaves? Which veterans absorbed a paycheck while younger players rotted on the bench? The draft lottery awaits, and with it, a chance to inject genuine talent into a system that's been treading water. <strong>The real work begins now - in the front office, not on the ice</strong>. Toronto needs answers about coaching, about player development, about whether this core can ever coalesce. The offseason is no longer a time to tinker. It's time to rebuild, honestly and completely.",
        "updated": "Updated May 12, 2026"
      },
